# THE NARRATION CORPUS — what the local model said, during the AUTHOR'S OWN PLAY. Written by
# `electron/corpus.mjs` as logs/corpus/narration.jsonl (+ .1). `logs/` above already covers it;
# this line is here so the intent is stated where somebody restructuring `logs/` will see it,
# and `src/dev/narrationCorpus.test.ts` asserts BOTH lines are present. THIS REPOSITORY IS
# PUBLIC — the corpus is never committed.
logs/corpus/

# API keys — the art-generation pipeline reads GOOGLE_API_KEY from here. NEVER commit a key.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Generated art candidates awaiting the engineer's pick. Only the chosen finals get committed.
# Created by `npm run art` (scripts/art/, PLAN.md #3) as art-candidates/<runId>/, holding the raw
# JPEGs, the keyed PNGs, the run manifest and the run log. NOTHING HAS BEEN GENERATED YET — a dry
# run creates no directory at all, and the shipped catalogue has no prompts to send.
# See docs/ART-BIBLE.md §1c.
art-candidates/

# Legacy Java/Python/Pixi ports: kept on disk for reference, not tracked by this
# repo (each carries its own nested .git history). Consult them locally.
.legacy/

# Personal planning documents. These are not game documents and are deliberately kept
